// v4 M-ext transport, Trap-cause + Debug-trigger sections. The writable M-ext
// CSRs the premium engine implements via the ALWAYS and TRIGGER gates must
// round-trip across the QEMU1 -> vsim handoff.
//
// Covered (HYBRID_M_EXT_CSR_LIST):
//   mdcause   -- detailed trap cause (ALWAYS gate; base Andes trap CSR)
//   tselect   -- trigger select index (TRIGGER gate; premium NDS_NUM_TRIGGER=2)
//   tdata2    -- trigger data 2 (match value/address)
//   mcontext  -- machine context
//
// Deliberately NOT exercised: tdata1/tcontrol. tdata1 holds a trigger's type +
// match/action bits, so writing a live value could arm a breakpoint that fires
// inside the ROI and halts vsim. They are transported + gated, but a round-trip
// test that writes them needs a disabled-trigger encoding; left to a dedicated
// trigger test. tdata2/tselect/mcontext alone never fire a trigger.
//
// Assertions mirror rt_csr_survival.S: in-ROI self-check (restore) + --verify
// (drain) under VERIFY=1.

